# REINFORCE++ at 32 x 8 without a turn cap: the no-turn-cap GRPO arm at
# 32 x 8 (68 updates) with Miles' --advantage-estimator reinforce_plus_plus. No critic, no GAE, no warmup: every token
# of a trial gets the trial's return (its reward: --kl-coef stays 0, the KL is our k3 loss term as in every arm, and
# gamma is Miles' default 1.0), whitened over the whole batch (--normalize-advantages, which Miles requires for this
# estimator; scripts/lib/container_main.sh passes it). GRPO's baseline is the mean of the task's own 8 samples, this
# one the batch's: a task whose 8 samples all scored 1 (e.g. failures repaired by the rewrite transform) still pushes
# them up. Source: third_party/miles/miles/backends/training_utils/loss/hub/advantages.py, math_utils.py:472.
#   CHAIN=train_eval ALGO=reinforce_plus_plus ARM=ota_train_full_rpp_b32 PRL_RUN_ID=<id> bash scripts/submit.sh
source "$PRL_ROOT/configs/arms/ota_train_full_noturncap_b32.env"
ADVANTAGE_ESTIMATOR=reinforce_plus_plus
NORMALIZE_ADVANTAGES=1
RUN_DIR=$PRL_EXT/runs/reinforce_plus_plus_ota_train_full_${PRL_RUN_ID:?set PRL_RUN_ID, shared by all jobs of the relay}
HARBOR_TRIALS_DIR=$RUN_DIR/harbor_trials/job_${JOB_ID}
